  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>zscore</keyword>
  <short_description>Standardized z-scores.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>Z = zscore(X)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>Z = zscore(X, flag)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>Z = zscore(X, flag, dim)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>Z = zscore(X, flag, vecdim)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>Z = zscore(X, flag, 'all')</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[Z, mu, sigma] = zscore(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>zscore</b> centers and scales numeric data by subtracting the mean and dividing by the standard deviation.</p>
    <p><b>flag</b> is 0 for sample standard deviation and 1 for population standard deviation. Samples containing <b>NaN</b> return <b>NaN</b> z-scores. Constant samples return zero z-scores.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[X = [1 2 3; 4 5 6];
[Z, mu, sigma] = zscore(X, 0, 1)]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
